    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=-3,-3,6$; $-3$ is a repeated root.",
      "worked": "Let the roots be $\\alpha,\\alpha,\\beta$.\n\nSum of roots:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\alpha+\\alpha+\\beta&=0\\\\\\beta&=-2\\alpha\\qquad(1)\\end{align*}$$\nProduct of roots:\n$$\\alpha^2\\beta=54\\qquad(2)$$\nSubstituting (1) into (2):\n$$\\begin{align*}-2\\alpha^3&=54\\\\\\alpha^3&=-27\\\\\\alpha&=-3\\\\\\beta&=6.\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore $x=-3,-3,6$, with $-3$ a repeated root.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
